item 1 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/1/measure".

item 1 measure is an assessment statement.

item 1 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 1 measure has the judgement "The requirements concerning the digital public service in question are aligned with the digital and sectoral policies (GDPR, Cybersecurity, Interoperability, Single Market, Customs, Pharmaceutical, Chemical, Education, Trade, Internal Market, Product Safety, Market Surveillance, Consumer Protection, Standardisation, Industrial Policy…)".

item 1 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeAlignmentMeasure".

item 1 measure has the description "Alignment with existing digital and sectorial policies.Please list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified".


item 2 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/2/measure".

item 2 measure is an assessment statement.

item 2 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 2 measure has the judgement "There are cross-border governance framework describing, among others, the roles and responsibilities involved in the delivery of digital public service (such as interoperability framework, EU Cybersecurity framework, eIDAS, recognised standards…).
There are competent authorities and/or single points of contact established and they have a mandate to supervise the digital public service concerned.
Digital by-default is prioritised and there is a mechanism for users to provide feedback on the digital public service (surveys, contact forms).".

item 2 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeOrganisationMeasure".

item 2 measure has the description "Organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services delivery.Please list the governance measures foreseen".


item 3 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/3/measure".

item 3 measure is an assessment statement.

item 3 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 3 measure has the judgement "The proposal uses commonly agreed guidelines and standards (depending on the policy and system the following are used: standardisation request for a data specification, standardisation request for data formats, use of open standards and specifications, setting up an expert group…)".

item 3 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeSharedMeasure".

item 3 measure has the description "Measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the data.Please list such measures".


item 4 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/4/measure".

item 4 measure is an assessment statement.

item 4 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 4 measure has the judgement "The possibility of machine-readable data has been addressed by the requirement and machine-to-machine interaction is addressed whenever possible. When appropriate and applicable, systems use standardized data models and ontologies for data representation and exchange, APIs…
Requirements refrain from imposing specific technical implementations or products.".

item 4 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeStandardsMeasure".

item 4 measure has the description "Use of commonly agreed open technical specifications and standards.Please list such measures".


